      "facts": "Original research on Qajar patronage discusses the prior dome’s approximate 16-meter height above the roof, octagonal transition, tall drum and gilding. It dates the renewed tiles to 2005."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://collections.si.edu/search/results.htm?fq=name%3A%22Islamic+Archives%22&fq=place%3A%22Qum+%28Iran%29%22&q=%22Religious+buildings%22",
      "facts": "The Smithsonian object records place two tall minarets at the Mirror Iwan and two smaller minarets at the opposite entrance. The associated archived images were not used."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://english.almaaref.org/post/2257/A-Glance-At-The-Holy-Shrine-of-Hadrat-Fatima-Masouma-(SA)-",
      "facts": "Describes the north Atiq court and Golden Iwan with its gilded pair, eastern Atabaki court and Mirror Iwan with two tall tiled towers, and the lower pair opposite it."
    }
